{"duration_api_ms":277319,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"40e935d8-be08-4ca3-b32f-830940ae1e1e","total_cost_usd":0.317074,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12460,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26723,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19501},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":26723,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":26723,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12460,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.317074,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":19501,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"No feasible design exists yet (0/20). Ten of the 20 rows are invalid geometry and none of the ten valid rows is feasible. The limits back-calculated from the margins are max_g <= 12 g and bondline <= 450 K. The mass-fraction limit is not shown, but it binds at about D = 3.0-3.2 m. Peak g rises with steepness of the flight-path angle (about 10.2 g at -2.6 deg, 12.7 g at -4.1 deg, 16-19 g below -6 deg). Bondline temperature falls with steeper angle and larger diameter. The geometry failures fit one rule: the fore cone has non-negative length only if cos(theta) <= 0.8/(2*b - 0.2). This assumes nose radius = b*D and shoulder radius = 0.1*D, and it reproduces the reported -22.8 mm for C-2e989122c857. For b = 0.5 any theta works, b = 0.7 needs theta >= 48.2, b = 1.0 needs theta >= 63.6, and b = 1.15 needs theta >= 68 deg. The plan is to sit at D of about 2.5-3.25 m, flight-path angle -1.85 to -3.8 deg, high bluntness and a cone angle safely above the validity bound.\",\"evidence\":[\"Limits from margins: C-ee99f55de428 has g 10.169 with margin 0.1526, so the g limit is 12. It has T 453.81 with margin -0.008466, so the bondline limit is 450 K.\",\"Geometry rule: valid rows (b, theta) are C-36f9165b9496 (0.87, 65), C-c72c38c9187a (0.64, 67.3), C-63aaa0985529 (0.52, 29.7) and C-50a0a474d0f6 (0.61, 42.5). Invalid rows are C-7fd3f4505944 (0.75, 36.4), C-0e7ec9742f84 (0.94, 55.1) and C-2e989122c857 (0.97, 59.8), which sits just inside the bound.\",\"Peak heat flux follows the Allen-Eggers form q ~ sqrt(sin(gamma)/(b*D^3)), calibrated on C-63aaa0985529 at 460k W/m2. It predicts C-ab9827dc6929 at about 480k (actual 478k), C-baa2f9e65f32 at about 338k (actual 330k) and C-50a0a474d0f6 at about 1.40M (actual 1.44M). Shallow entries run higher than this form: C-f97dae207371 is +22% and C-ee99f55de428 is +8%.\",\"Bondline fit for D >= 2.3: T - 300 ~ 104.4*sqrt(q/460k)*(|gamma|/4.1)^-0.4. It reproduces C-ab9827dc6929 (403), C-36f9165b9496 (about 404 vs 400.7), C-26bc5a06b4e4 (about 376 vs 373.6) and C-f97dae207371 (about 430 vs 435.9).\",\"Heatshield mass ratio (1 - margin) is about c*D^2 with c about 0.11 at theta 30-38 (C-63aaa0985529, C-f97dae207371) and about 0.089 at theta 65-68 (C-36f9165b9496, C-12010dd082dd). D must therefore stay below about 3.0 m at low theta and about 3.2 m at high theta.\",\"Peak g: C-f97dae207371 gives 9.5 at -1.85 deg, C-ee99f55de428 gives 10.2 at -2.64 deg, C-63aaa0985529 gives 12.67 at -4.1 deg and C-ab9827dc6929 gives 13.06 at -4.26 deg. The 12 g limit is therefore near -3.7 deg, so I target -3.0 to -3.6 deg with a boundary probe at -3.8 deg.\",\"The hypervolume reference is (2.5e6, 450), so both bondline temperature and heat flux are worth reducing. Large nose radius (high b, large D) cuts q and T together. This is the direction of the proposals.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heat flux scales with sqrt(rho_peak/Rn). Peak-heating density scales with ballistic coefficient (1/D^2) times sin(gamma), and nose radius is b*D. Large D and large b therefore lower q. Bondline temperature follows total heat load, which falls with steeper entry (shorter pulse) and lower q. Peak g rises with steepness and pushes back toward shallow angles. Mass fraction limits D, and a larger cone angle lowers it by reducing shield area. So the best feasible region should be the largest D that passes mass, high b, high theta above the geometric floor, and gamma near the g limit. Shallower gamma with large b trades higher T for lower q and extends the front.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The heat-flux and bondline surrogates are fitted to about 10 points, and the Allen-Eggers form is prior knowledge that I checked against the data. Extrapolating to b above 0.9 is unverified, because shoulder or torus heating and drag coefficient may change. The g-versus-gamma dependence near -3.5 deg is interpolated between sparse rows, and the mass-fraction limit is only estimated from c*D^2 trends. The geometry validity rule is inferred, not given, so the b = 1.15 proposals at theta 70 are close to it. Shallow-entry heat flux may be higher than my correction assumes. Cone-angle effects on drag are ignored.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Large D and high bluntness with theta 66 (above the 63.6 floor for b=1.0). Aims for low q and low T at gamma -3.5, just inside the 12 g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":388,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Best-guess anchor for the low-q, low-T corner. It tests the high-b extrapolation and the g estimate near -3.5 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 0.8 with theta 58 (floor 55.2) and D 3.05 to keep mass fraction under the limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.05,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":58.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":333000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the b=0.8 gap between the b=0.5 and b=1.0 proposals at the same gamma, showing how b maps to q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.0, b 0.9 and theta 64 (floor 60), with gamma -3.4 for extra g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":317000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safer-margin feasible candidate close to the expected front, likely to yield the first feasible point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D 3.15 with theta 62 and moderate b 0.7 (floor 48.2). Mass fraction should be about 0.90 of the limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":329000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mass-fraction limit near D 3.15 at high theta. That limit decides how far D can go.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D 2.8 with b 1.1 and theta 68 (floor 66.4). Gives large mass-fraction margin and a large nose radius.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":323000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether bluntness can replace diameter for cutting q and T while staying comfortably inside the mass limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Aggressive bluntness b 1.15 at theta 70, close to the validity floor of about 68.7 deg, with D 2.9 and gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the extreme-blunt corner and the geometry rule at its edge. The reduced model may miss shoulder heating, so a higher-fidelity look is worthwhile.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Low bluntness 0.5 (valid at any theta) at D 3.1, theta 60 and gamma -3.6, near the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":417000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Quantifies the benefit of bluntness by comparison with the b=1.0 design at nearly the same D and gamma. Also tests g at -3.6 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate gamma -3.0 gives a comfortable g margin, with D 3.0, b 0.6 and theta 55 (floor 36.9).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":55.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":368000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A safely feasible mid-gamma point to anchor the g and T interpolation between -1.85 and -4.1 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.7, b 0.8 and theta 60 (floor 55.2). Large mass margin with a medium nose radius.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.7,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":388000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how much q and T are lost by using D 2.7 instead of about 3.1 when mass margin is comfortable.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Small D 2.5 with b 1.0 and theta 66. This is the smallest-D point in the batch and checks that large Rn compensates for a small capsule.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.5,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":401000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the D dependence at fixed b, theta and gamma against the D=3.1 anchor, testing the D^-1.5 heat-flux scaling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Low bluntness 0.4 with D 3.2 and theta 68. The high theta is meant to bring mass fraction under the limit, unlike C-ab9827dc6929, which failed by 0.4% at theta 52.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.4,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":432000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether raising theta really recovers mass margin at D 3.2. It is a small edit of the nearly feasible C-ab9827dc6929.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f97dae207371\",\"rationale\":\"C-f97dae207371 failed only on mass fraction (-0.127) at theta 37.6. Raising theta to 65 should cut the shield ratio by about 15-20%, which gives a shallow-entry feasible point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":376000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":436,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A single-variable change that isolates the effect of theta on mass fraction, q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f97dae207371\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow gamma -2.2 with large b 1.0 and D 3.1 targets low peak heat flux, extending the front to low q at the cost of higher T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the low-q end of the trade-off. Shallow-entry heat flux ran higher than the simple scaling in the data, so the correction factor is uncertain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma -2.8 with D 2.9, b 0.9 and theta 64 (floor 60). Fills the middle of the q-versus-T trade-off.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":318000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage between the shallow and -3.5 deg designs and locates the T-versus-gamma slope for large b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Boundary probe at gamma -3.8 with the same shape as the first anchor. I expect g of about 12.1, marginally infeasible, but it would give lower T if it passed.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":303000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":387,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g = 12 boundary in gamma for a blunt high-theta shape. High drag may lower g, so it could be feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the first anchor (D 3.1, b 1.0, gamma -3.5) but theta 70 instead of 66. Isolates the theta effect on g, q, T and mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":388,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Paired comparison with the theta-66 anchor to measure the cone-angle effect on drag, g and mass fraction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.0, b 0.5 and theta 68, a low-blunt, high-theta design at gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":425000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A pure b-effect comparison against the b=0.9 design, and a safely valid geometry for a feasible reference.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to 3.25 with b 0.9 and theta 70 to test the upper edge of the mass-fraction limit. Predicted mass ratio is about 0.91 of the limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":388,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the maximum usable diameter. If it passes, it dominates the smaller-D designs on both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.6 with b 1.15, theta 70 and gamma -3.0. Small D with very large nose radius and a comfortable g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":330000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A second extreme-blunt sample with a different D and gamma, to check whether the sqrt(1/(b*D^3)) scaling holds at b > 1.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-blunt b 0.7 with theta 52 (floor 48.2) at D 3.0 and gamma -3.6. A moderate-theta point checks the theta trend for mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":52.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":370000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the design space at moderate theta and adds a second sample at -3.6 deg to refine the g and T model near the boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":216640,"type":"result","duration_ms":277380,"uuid":"a19db2d0-1bc4-4538-8104-80f8615faf04","ttft_stream_ms":1280,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":1281,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
